    "Inspect the actual pinned-SDK forwarding wrapper and invocation JSONL. Match all six order publish invocations to the real SDK executable and PublishAot=true. The wrapper adds ordinary single-process/build-server options and forwards with os.execv; it does not synthesize SDK output.",
    "Read VerificationDatabase.cs and Program.cs at the reviewed commit: SQLite uses a fresh file database; PostgreSQL requires an actual connection, creates a fresh database and drops it after the run. The consumer throws if RuntimeFeature.IsDynamicCodeSupported is true and executes the recorded migration/query/write/transaction checks.",
    "Independently re-extract each of the four tutorial code fences from the actual candidate README or the reviewed source guide, reconstruct the two namespace wrappers, and recompute original source, fence and compiled-source hashes.",
    "Compare original/edited source sets and hashes: only Models.cs changes. Independently reproduce the exact DTO source edit from the committed Models.cs and match its recorded hash; compare unchanged tutorial and scaffold hashes, distinct AOT executable hashes and identical packaged native hashes."
